<!-- [WOLF TERRAFORM 2026-10-23] The Terraform window (wolffloaterterraform.cpp). Paul: "where is the extra terraforming tools you
     know we were going to enhance it based on other terraforming applications". Design: firestorm/region-terrain-work/
     terraforming-tools/DESIGN.md (3.2 the tools, 3.3 the preview, 3.5 the menus, 3.6 the look).
     Persona: Jimmy, a region owner building a sim, who wants level pads, ramps, roads, rivers and beaches fast and to take a
     mistake back, without learning an expert tool. Story: "I pick a tool, click or draw on the ground, see what will change, press
     Apply, watch it work, and can take it back."
     Flow: 1. pick a tool tile -> click (or draw) on the ground; the hint line says what -> 2. its two or three settings (the rest
     under More options, closed) -> 3. the preview in the world (red = cut, green = fill), Apply and the summary under it (the mole plate lies over the summary and the status line, never over Apply or Stop) -> the mole plate
     while it works -> 4. the step in History, Undo / Redo.
     Layout: 596 high with More options closed; More options adds 64 at the bottom (WolfFloaterTerraform::relayout). The burrow
     look (wolfburrow.cpp): fixed colours on fixed paint, so every text pair keeps its contrast in every skin
     (region-terrain-work/cave-lights/check/burrow_contrast.py: CREAM on a plate 13.4:1, MUTED 9.1:1, DIS 6.8:1, CREAM on stone
     8.1:1+, INK on amber 6.7:1+). The tool tiles' pictures and words are painted (paintBurrow). -->
